Okay... Joey, why don't you pick it up where Renata left off ?

44
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.750
Now, this is a hard part.

45
00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.160
So take your time.

46
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.870
Oh, boy, yeah. This is-- This looks tough.

47
00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.440
"The bell rang and the students all went to  the auditorium with their teacher." Boom !

48
00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.870
That's right, Boris. You heard it...

49
00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.300
"Auditorium" !

50
00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.110
I am so lucky to be with the smartest boy in class.

51
00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.220
Some words are so tug.

52
00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:37.930
"Tug" ?

53
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.290
Oh, remember, I told you the GH sometimes sounds like an F.

54
00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.790
It's "tough". Like "rough" or "laugh".

55
00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.810
Oh, Joey, make love to me tonigh-F-t.

56
00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.320
That ...is good English.

57
00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.660
Okay...

58
00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:02.580
I'd like everybody to take out their homework on the subjunctive tense.

59
00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.840
You didn't do it ??

60
00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.270
I got it.

61
00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:10.850
If the present tense of the verb to be is "I am"...

62
00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.900
then the subjunctive tense is "if I..." ?

63
00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.400
Joey.

64
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.850
"If I was."

65
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.780
That's not correct.

66
00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.390
It's, uh... "if I were."

67
00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.160
Very good, Boris.

68
00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:28.330
[Laughter]

69
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.160
🎵Joey are stupid. 🎶

70
00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.390
"Joey IS stupid", Renata !

71
00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.610
[Applause]

72
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.730
[Music]

73
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.100
Ah, Maria... I totally forgot.

74
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.340
I can't go on a picnic today, I have to study.

75
00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.630
But why ? It's just a stupid class.

76
00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.540
"A stupid class" !?!

77
00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.380
Maria, my studies are very important to me.

78
00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.210
Yes, but there is a nice park to go to.

79
00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:01.380
Okay... first of all, you don't end a sentence with the preposition.

80
00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.390
Okay, that is wrong.

81
00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.960
In fact, lately, everything about you is wrong.

82
00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.180
Except for your awesome, awesome body !

83
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.910
And I'm afraid, I'm gonna have to say goodbye Maria.

84
00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.080
- But what about us ? - You know, he said goodbye.

85
00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.490
[SPANISH] Pues ¡ Quédate aquí con tu mujerzuela !

86
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.000
- What'd she say ? - She thinks I'm your whore.

87
00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.900
Can anyone give me an example  of a multiple homonym ?

88
00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:32.930
I can !

89
00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.570
"They're" meaning "they are",

90
00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:43.440
"their" meaning group possessive... and "there" meaning "in that place".

91
00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.780
That's very good, Joey.

92
00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:49.630
- Joey wins the prize. - YES !!

93
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.820
Thank you. I would like to share another American phrase with all of you.

94
00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.260
Uh, "SUCK IT !"

95
00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.810
Have fun studying, Joey.
